config SMART_HOME_VOICE_TTS
    bool "Agent reply voice announcement (TTS)"
    depends on ESP32P4_FUNCTION_EV_BOARD_AUDIO_ES8311
    depends on NETUTILS_CJSON
    default n
    help
      Announce agent replies through the ES8311 speaker.  Adds the shared
      PCM16 mono voice player, the cloud TTS synthesis client (OpenAI
      compatible /v1/audio/speech), a queued announcement service and the
      chat-screen auto-announce hook.  The announce switch is persisted in
      /data/smart_home/voice.json; API keys are read from secrets.json.

if SMART_HOME_VOICE_TTS

config SMART_HOME_TTS_AUDIO_MAX_BYTES
    int "Maximum TTS audio response buffer"
    default 1048576
    range 65536 2097152
    help
      Upper bound of the PSRAM buffer holding one synthesized WAV
      response.  For speech-style backends (binary WAV) 1 MiB is about
      32 s at 16 kHz PCM16 mono; for chat-style backends (MiMo) the
      response is JSON-wrapped base64 (~4/3 larger), so the effective
      audio cap is about 768 KiB.

