config SMART_HOME_TTS_SMOKE
    bool "TTS pipeline smoke command"
    depends on SMART_HOME_VOICE_TTS
    default n
    help
      Build the tts_smoke NSH command for the voice announcement bring-up.
      It plays a raw PCM16 mono file through the same shared player as the
      announcement service (play subcommand) and synthesizes plus plays a
      short text once the TTS backend is configured (speak subcommand).  It
      deliberately starts no LVGL UI and touches no agent state.

if SMART_HOME_TTS_SMOKE

config SMART_HOME_TTS_SMOKE_STACKSIZE
    int "TTS smoke command stack size"
    default 32768
    range 16384 65536
    help
      The speak subcommand runs the full mbedTLS synthesis request on the
      command stack.  mbedTLS does not fit in the 8 KiB NSH default (the
      handshake overflows and hard-freezes the system before any error
      can print); this follows the agent chat worker budget.

endif

config SMART_HOME_VOICE_ASR
    bool "Agent voice input (ASR, MiMo-V2.5-ASR)"
    depends on ESP32P4_FUNCTION_EV_BOARD_AUDIO_ES8311
    depends on NETUTILS_CJSON
    default n
    help
      Add push-to-talk voice input to the chat screen.  A shared capture
      service owns /dev/audio/pcm_in0 (16 kHz PCM16 mono) and feeds both
      ASR sessions and (later) the KWS listener.  Recordings are
      recognized by the MiMo-V2.5-ASR cloud API (OpenAI-compatible chat
      completions with base64 WAV input_audio) and the transcript is
      auto-submitted to the agent.  The voice-input switch and language
      (zh/en/auto) are persisted in /data/smart_home/asr.json; the API
      key reuses model_api_keys.mimo from secrets.json.

