config SMART_HOME_VAD
    bool "Energy-based VAD on the shared audio capture path"
    depends on ESP32P4_FUNCTION_EV_BOARD_AUDIO_ES8311
    default n
    help
      Add an integer-only voice activity detector to the shared capture
      service.  It runs on every captured frame before the registered
      consumer, so it keeps working while ASR and KWS swap the consumer
      slot.  Once speech has been seen, a sustained silence ends the
      recording early, which turns push-to-talk into "speak and stop".

      The detector uses a 20 ms frame with a 10 ms hop, a slow/fast
      adaptive noise floor, a relative threshold and an absolute energy
      floor, then a start/hangover state machine.  No floating point and
      no libm calls are used, which matters on the current P4 build
      (single core, soft float).

if SMART_HOME_VAD

config SMART_HOME_VAD_RATIO_PCT
    int "Speech threshold relative to the noise floor (percent)"
    default 400
    range 150 2000
    help
      A frame counts as speech when its energy exceeds the tracked noise
      floor by this percentage.  400 means +6 dB.  Raise it in noisy
      rooms, lower it for far-field talkers.

config SMART_HOME_VAD_MIN_ENERGY
    int "Absolute frame energy floor"
    default 400
    range 0 100000
    help
      Frames below this energy are never speech, which keeps the
      detector quiet on digital silence where the noise floor can
      collapse towards zero.  Energy is sum(x^2) >> 12 over a 20 ms
      frame at 16 kHz; 400 corresponds to an RMS of roughly 90 LSB.

config SMART_HOME_VAD_INIT_FRAMES
    int "Noise floor initialisation frames"
    default 10
    range 1 200
    help
      During the first N frames the noise floor follows the minimum
      observed energy, so starting a recording on speech does not bias
      the floor upwards.

config SMART_HOME_VAD_START_FRAMES
    int "Consecutive speech frames required to start"
    default 3
    range 1 50
    help
      Each frame advances 10 ms, so the default needs 30 ms of speech.

config SMART_HOME_VAD_END_FRAMES
    int "Consecutive silence frames required to end"
    default 30
    range 1 300
    help
      Hangover before the detector reports the end of speech.  The
      default is 300 ms, which keeps short pauses between words from
      splitting an utterance.

config SMART_HOME_VAD_AUTOSTOP_SILENCE_MS
    int "Recording auto-stop silence in ms"
    default 500
    range 0 5000
    help
      After speech has been detected, the ASR recording ends when this
      much additional silence follows the detector's end-of-speech
      event.  0 disables the early stop and keeps the fixed duration.

endif

config SMART_HOME_KWS
    bool "Resident KWS wake-word service (wake_large int8)"
    depends on ESP32P4_FUNCTION_EV_BOARD_AUDIO_ES8311
    depends on TFLITEMICRO
    default n
    help
      Offline always-on wake-word detection with the wake_large int8
      ds_cnn_s3 model (37,408 bytes).  The ESP32-P4 has no ESP-NN
      backend, so TFLite Micro reference kernels are used.  A resident
      service consumes the shared capture service, keeps a 2.5 s PCM
      ring, computes the 124x40x3 feature front-end and reports wake
      hits through a callback with threshold voting and cooldown.
      NOTE: the feature front-end constants are provisional until they
      are verified value-by-value against the training pipeline; treat
      on-device wake rates as unvalidated until then.

if SMART_HOME_KWS

config SMART_HOME_KWS_ARENA_SIZE
    int "KWS tensor arena size"
    default 393216
    range 65536 3145728
    help
      PSRAM buffer reserved for TFLite Micro tensors of wake_large.
      The service reports the actual arena use after AllocateTensors.

      The model needs about 199 KB on the target (conv/depthwise output
      tensors alone total ~516 KB across 4 conv + 3 dw nodes when the
      arena is shared; the reference path allocates ~199 KB). The old
      196608 default was below the real requirement, so the resident
      service failed at AllocateTensors with -ENOMEM. 393216 leaves
      headroom for the ESP-NN path, which additionally requests a
      filter copy and scratch per node.

config SMART_HOME_KWS_WORKER_STACKSIZE
    int "KWS inference worker stack size"
    default 32768
    range 8192 131072
    help
      The worker runs the C++ TFLite Micro interpreter plus the feature
      front-end on its own stack. 12 KB was too tight once ESP-NN and the
      full front-end are enabled; 32 KB leaves room without depending on
      unmeasured luck. Keep this independent from the smoke command stack.

config SMART_HOME_KWS_INTERVAL_MS
    int "KWS inference interval in ms"
    default 500
    range 100 2000
    help
      How often the 2.5 s sliding window is re-evaluated.  Start
      conservative; tighten only after kws_smoke reports the real
      reference-kernel Invoke latency on the target.

config SMART_HOME_KWS_THRESHOLD
    int "KWS wake threshold in per-mille"
    default 750
    range 1 1000
    help
      Starting point from the offline threshold sweep (0.75); real-room
      false-wake tuning must be done on the device.

config SMART_HOME_KWS_COOLDOWN_MS
    int "KWS wake cooldown in ms"
    default 3000
    range 500 30000

endif

config SMART_HOME_KWS_SMOKE
    bool "KWS model smoke/benchmark command"
    depends on TFLITEMICRO
    default n
    help
      Build the kws_smoke NSH command.  It validates the TFLite model,
      operator registration, tensor contract and arena use, then
      benchmarks Invoke() with a deterministic int8 feature buffer.
      It opens no audio device and runs no recognition.

if SMART_HOME_KWS_SMOKE

config SMART_HOME_KWS_SMOKE_ARENA_SIZE
    int "KWS smoke tensor arena size"
    default 393216
    range 65536 3145728

config SMART_HOME_KWS_SMOKE_STACKSIZE
    int "KWS smoke command stack size"
    default 12288
    range 8192 32768

endif

